              "DATADOG_CONFIDENCE_REASON:Source: The @CurrentUsername annotation provides the username. Sink: The File constructor on line 32 takes the username as part of the file path. Dataflow: The untrusted username flows directly into the file path construction without validation. Sanitization: No sanitization is performed on the username. An attacker who can control their assigned username (e.g., via registration inputs) can use characters like '..' to perform a path traversal attack and write/overwrite files outside the intended directory. This is a path traversal vulnerability."
